Drop the leading "::" from the namespaced custom widget class.

Qt 6.12's uic rejects a custom widget class name that starts with "::"
("Invalid class name"), so the dictionary tool UI cannot be compiled.
Upstream google/mozc uses the same class name without the leading "::",
which is what uic expects.

--- a/src/gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_tool.ui
+++ b/src/gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_tool.ui
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
        <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
       </property>
       <widget class="QListWidget" name="dic_list_"/>
-      <widget class="::mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget" name="dic_content_"/>
+      <widget class="mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget" name="dic_content_"/>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
    <container>1</container>
   </customwidget>
   <customwidget>
-   <class>::mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget</class>
+   <class>mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget</class>
    <extends>QTableWidget</extends>
    <header>gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_content_table_widget.h</header>
   </customwidget>
